    "description": "Natural Mineral Display Specimen\nThis item is a section showing natural mineral characteristics. The outer surface is rough with an earthy brown color and natural textures. The inner section is  smooth, displaying shades of dark gray, brown, and tan. The center features a cavity or depression, which may/may not include mineral deposits. The specimen is unbranded and in natural, unaltered condition with minor wear and surface imperfections consistent with geological samples. Suitable for collectors of  minerals or natural history. Wares: May have  gentle wear. May have markings, staining, scuff marks, scratches or  damage that was missed when photographing. May have discoloration/fading. May have rips/tearing. May have chipping and or paint loss. May be an incomplete set. May have  missing pieces/broken pieces. May have cracks. May have previous stickers on the item(s) from previous storing or use.  May have a smell from being stored and may have discoloration. Packaging may have damage. Product may need cleaned/repaired or restored. Sold as is.\nDetails\nThis is a pre-owned, donated item being sold “AS IS.\nItems may show wear consistent with usage and age, such as: discoloration; scratches; scuffs; dents; cracks; chips; holes; loose threads and stitches; edge and corner wear; box wear; oxidation; dirt; dust; other residue; owner-added markings; and signs of repair such as tape and glue.\nLot items may not contain all original parts or accessories and may have been outfitted with replacement pieces and/or modifications by previous owners\nBulk lots are not returnable. Due to the volume of items that flow through our eCommerce department, customer service requests to test items may be denied.\nAny certificates and markers of authenticity referenced in this listing are assertions of authenticity by the manufacturer, production company, or a third party, and not a guarantee of authenticity by Goodwill.\nItems and autographs without certificates or 